        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs an exception object from a status value. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If <computeroutput>status</computeroutput> is <computeroutput>0</computeroutput>, the exception is still created with an empty error message. Otherwise, the constructor initializes the error message (later accessible with <computeroutput><ref refid="classcuda_1_1experimental_1_1stf_1_1cuda__exception_1a5d1c26dcc11b2bcfe563e638e33d2360" kindref="member">what()</ref></computeroutput>) appropriately.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>status type, can be <computeroutput>cudaError_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>cublasStatus_t</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>cusolverStatus_t</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
